Notes:
- Matches one generic-password item (`kSecClassGenericPassword`). Internet passwords use `kSecClassInternetPassword` + server/protocol attrs instead.
- Caller must be allowed by that item’s ACL; otherwise you get `errSecAuthFailed` / `-128` (user canceled), not a silent read.
- Don’t print passwords into logs or shell history if you can avoid it.
